{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FXwBWTtpxGRc8sHxfnrNZ1","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# CLAUDE.md\n     2→\n     3→This file provides guidance to Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with code in this repository.\n     4→\n     5→## Project Overview\n     6→\n     7→**Audiobook Prep** is an AI-powered manuscript analysis tool for audiobook narrators. It analyzes books to extract structure (chapters), characters with aliases, pronunciation guidance, and generates summaries. The tool is local-first and uses a multi-agent architecture with support for multiple LLM providers (Ollama, OpenAI, Anthropic).\n     8→\n     9→## Common Commands\n    10→\n    11→```bash\n    12→# Install (editable mode with dev dependencies)\n    13→pip install -e \".[dev]\"\n    14→python -m spacy download en_core_web_lg\n    15→\n    16→# Run analysis via CLI\n    17→audiobook-prep analyze book.pdf\n    18→audiobook-prep analyze book.pdf --output result.json --html report.html\n    19→audiobook-prep analyze book.pdf --tui  # Opens interactive TUI after analysis\n    20→\n    21→# Run GUI\n    22→./launch_gui.sh  # or: python -m src.gui.desktop\n    23→\n    24→# Run tests\n    25→pytest  # Uses tests/ directory per pyproject.toml\n    26→\n    27→# Code formatting\n    28→black src/\n    29→ruff check src/\n    30→```\n    31→\n    32→## Architecture\n    33→\n    34→### Multi-Agent Pipeline\n    35→\n    36→The system uses specialized agents that wrap consensus-based pipelines:\n    37→\n    38→```\n    39→Input File → Ingestion → StructureAgent → CharacterAgent → SummaryAgent → PronunciationAgent → Export\n    40→                              ↓                ↓                ↓                ↓\n    41→                        ChapterMap      CharacterMap    ChapterSummaries   PronunciationMap\n    42→```\n    43→\n    44→Each agent:\n    45→- Wraps a pipeline with multiple \"proposers\" that generate candidates\n    46→- Uses consensus to select best results\n    47→- Implements self-verification with confidence scoring\n    48→- Can use a different LLM model (configured via `OrchestratorConfig`)\n    49→\n    50→### Key Modules\n    51→\n    52→| Module | Purpose |\n    53→|--------|---------|\n    54→| `src/analyzer.py` | Main orchestrator - runs all agents sequentially |\n    55→| `src/agents/` | Agent infrastructure (base.py, config.py) and implementations |\n    56→| `src/pipeline/` | Analysis pipelines (chapter_detection, character_extraction, etc.) |\n    57→| `src/pipeline/llm.py` | Unified LLM client for Ollama/OpenAI/Anthropic |\n    58→| `src/ingestion/` | Document parsers (PDF, EPUB, DOCX, TXT) |\n    59→| `src/gui/desktop.py` | Tkinter GUI with model management |\n    60→| `src/gui/tui.py` | Textual-based terminal UI for result browsing |\n    61→| `src/models.py` | Pydantic data models (AnalysisResult, Character, etc.) |\n    62→\n    63→### Agent System\n    64→\n    65→Agents are defined in `src/agents/` and follow this pattern:\n    66→\n    67→```python\n    68→class Agent(ABC):\n    69→    @property\n    70→    def name(self) -> str: ...\n    71→    def run(self, context: AgentContext) -> AgentResult: ...\n    72→    def verify(self, result: AgentResult) -> VerificationResult: ...\n    73→```\n    74→\n    75→Multi-model configuration allows different models per agent:\n    76→```python\n    77→from src.agents.config import OrchestratorConfig, AgentConfig, create_optimized_config\n    78→\n    79→# Auto-optimize based on available models\n    80→config = create_optimized_config(available_models=[\"qwen2.5:72b\", \"qwen2.5:7b\"])\n    81→\n    82→# Or manual per-agent configuration\n    83→config = OrchestratorConfig(default_model=\"llama3.2\")\n    84→config.set_agent_config(\"characters\", AgentConfig(model=\"qwen2.5:72b\"))\n    85→```\n    86→\n    87→See `src/agents/config.py` for `RECOMMENDED_AGENT_MODELS` with optimal settings per agent type.\n    88→\n    89→### LLM Integration\n    90→\n    91→`LLMClient` in `src/pipeline/llm.py` provides a unified interface:\n    92→```python\n    93→client = LLMClient(LLMConfig.ollama(model=\"llama3.2\"))\n    94→client = LLMClient(LLMConfig.openai(model=\"gpt-4o-mini\"))\n    95→client = LLMClient(LLMConfig.anthropic(model=\"claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022\"))\n    96→```\n    97→\n    98→Features automatic thinking tag stripping for reasoning models (DeepSeek-R1, QwQ).\n    99→\n   100→## Data Flow\n   101→\n   102→1. **Ingestion**: Extract text from PDF/EPUB/DOCX/TXT via `src/ingestion/`\n   103→2. **Refinement**: Normalize text, fix spacing/encoding via `src/ingestion/refine.py`\n   104→3. **Structure**: StructureAgent detects chapters using regex + LLM consensus\n   105→4. **Characters**: CharacterAgent extracts names via NER + LLM, resolves aliases\n   106→5. **Summaries**: SummaryAgent generates per-chapter summaries\n   107→6. **Pronunciation**: PronunciationAgent flags proper nouns, foreign words, homographs\n   108→7. **Export**: JSON output, HTML report, or interactive TUI\n   109→\n   110→## Important Files\n   111→\n   112→- `docs/AGENT_ARCHITECTURE.md` - Detailed architecture documentation and roadmap\n   113→- `src/agents/config.py` - Agent configuration, model recommendations\n   114→- `src/pipeline/metrics.py` - Profiling and metrics collection\n   115→- Entry points defined in `pyproject.toml`: `audiobook-prep` (CLI), `audiobook-prep-gui` (GUI)\n   116→\n   117→## Coding Standards\n   118→\n   119→### No Novel-Specific Hardcoding\n   120→\n   121→NEVER include examples from specific novels in prompts or validation logic. The system must work for ANY novel without bias toward specific works.\n   122→\n   123→**Examples of what NOT to do:**\n   124→- ❌ \"Tom Buchanan and Daisy Buchanan are DIFFERENT people (husband and wife)\"\n   125→- ❌ \"Jay Gatsby should be merged with Mr. Gatsby\"\n   126→\n   127→**Use generic guidance instead:**\n   128→- ✅ \"Characters who share a last name but have different first names are typically different people (e.g., spouses, siblings)\"\n   129→- ✅ \"A full name and a first-name-only reference may be the same person\"\n   130→\n   131→---\n   132→\n   133→## Development Notes\n   134→\n   135→- Python 3.10+ required\n   136→- spaCy `en_core_web_lg` model required for NER\n   137→- At least one LLM provider (Ollama, OpenAI, or Anthropic) required for LLM features\n   138→- Current branch: `feature/agent-infrastructure` (Phase 3 complete, Phase 4 planned)\n   139→- `Output/` directory is gitignored but created during analysis\n   140→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bfefdb08-6e29-453e-a2e4-75379a31713f","uuid":"1396db95-345d-4018-9c26-e379b9cedc5e","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/zacharymandrews/Tools/audiobook_agent/CLAUDE.md","content":"# CLAUDE.md\n\nThis file provides guidance to Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with code in this repository.\n\n## Project Overview\n\n**Audiobook Prep** is an AI-powered manuscript analysis tool for audiobook narrators. It analyzes books to extract structure (chapters), characters with aliases, pronunciation guidance, and generates summaries. The tool is local-first and uses a multi-agent architecture with support for multiple LLM providers (Ollama, OpenAI, Anthropic).\n\n## Common Commands\n\n```bash\n# Install (editable mode with dev dependencies)\npip install -e \".[dev]\"\npython -m spacy download en_core_web_lg\n\n# Run analysis via CLI\naudiobook-prep analyze book.pdf\naudiobook-prep analyze book.pdf --output result.json --html report.html\naudiobook-prep analyze book.pdf --tui  # Opens interactive TUI after analysis\n\n# Run GUI\n./launch_gui.sh  # or: python -m src.gui.desktop\n\n# Run tests\npytest  # Uses tests/ directory per pyproject.toml\n\n# Code formatting\nblack src/\nruff check src/\n```\n\n## Architecture\n\n### Multi-Agent Pipeline\n\nThe system uses specialized agents that wrap consensus-based pipelines:\n\n```\nInput File → Ingestion → StructureAgent → CharacterAgent → SummaryAgent → PronunciationAgent → Export\n                              ↓                ↓                ↓                ↓\n                        ChapterMap      CharacterMap    ChapterSummaries   PronunciationMap\n```\n\nEach agent:\n- Wraps a pipeline with multiple \"proposers\" that generate candidates\n- Uses consensus to select best results\n- Implements self-verification with confidence scoring\n- Can use a different LLM model (configured via `OrchestratorConfig`)\n\n### Key Modules\n\n| Module | Purpose |\n|--------|---------|\n| `src/analyzer.py` | Main orchestrator - runs all agents sequentially |\n| `src/agents/` | Agent infrastructure (base.py, config.py) and implementations |\n| `src/pipeline/` | Analysis pipelines (chapter_detection, character_extraction, etc.) |\n| `src/pipeline/llm.py` | Unified LLM client for Ollama/OpenAI/Anthropic |\n| `src/ingestion/` | Document parsers (PDF, EPUB, DOCX, TXT) |\n| `src/gui/desktop.py` | Tkinter GUI with model management |\n| `src/gui/tui.py` | Textual-based terminal UI for result browsing |\n| `src/models.py` | Pydantic data models (AnalysisResult, Character, etc.) |\n\n### Agent System\n\nAgents are defined in `src/agents/` and follow this pattern:\n\n```python\nclass Agent(ABC):\n    @property\n    def name(self) -> str: ...\n    def run(self, context: AgentContext) -> AgentResult: ...\n    def verify(self, result: AgentResult) -> VerificationResult: ...\n```\n\nMulti-model configuration allows different models per agent:\n```python\nfrom src.agents.config import OrchestratorConfig, AgentConfig, create_optimized_config\n\n# Auto-optimize based on available models\nconfig = create_optimized_config(available_models=[\"qwen2.5:72b\", \"qwen2.5:7b\"])\n\n# Or manual per-agent configuration\nconfig = OrchestratorConfig(default_model=\"llama3.2\")\nconfig.set_agent_config(\"characters\", AgentConfig(model=\"qwen2.5:72b\"))\n```\n\nSee `src/agents/config.py` for `RECOMMENDED_AGENT_MODELS` with optimal settings per agent type.\n\n### LLM Integration\n\n`LLMClient` in `src/pipeline/llm.py` provides a unified interface:\n```python\nclient = LLMClient(LLMConfig.ollama(model=\"llama3.2\"))\nclient = LLMClient(LLMConfig.openai(model=\"gpt-4o-mini\"))\nclient = LLMClient(LLMConfig.anthropic(model=\"claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022\"))\n```\n\nFeatures automatic thinking tag stripping for reasoning models (DeepSeek-R1, QwQ).\n\n## Data Flow\n\n1. **Ingestion**: Extract text from PDF/EPUB/DOCX/TXT via `src/ingestion/`\n2. **Refinement**: Normalize text, fix spacing/encoding via `src/ingestion/refine.py`\n3. **Structure**: StructureAgent detects chapters using regex + LLM consensus\n4. **Characters**: CharacterAgent extracts names via NER + LLM, resolves aliases\n5. **Summaries**: SummaryAgent generates per-chapter summaries\n6. **Pronunciation**: PronunciationAgent flags proper nouns, foreign words, homographs\n7. **Export**: JSON output, HTML report, or interactive TUI\n\n## Important Files\n\n- `docs/AGENT_ARCHITECTURE.md` - Detailed architecture documentation and roadmap\n- `src/agents/config.py` - Agent configuration, model recommendations\n- `src/pipeline/metrics.py` - Profiling and metrics collection\n- Entry points defined in `pyproject.toml`: `audiobook-prep` (CLI), `audiobook-prep-gui` (GUI)\n\n## Coding Standards\n\n### No Novel-Specific Hardcoding\n\nNEVER include examples from specific novels in prompts or validation logic. The system must work for ANY novel without bias toward specific works.\n\n**Examples of what NOT to do:**\n- ❌ \"Tom Buchanan and Daisy Buchanan are DIFFERENT people (husband and wife)\"\n- ❌ \"Jay Gatsby should be merged with Mr. Gatsby\"\n\n**Use generic guidance instead:**\n- ✅ \"Characters who share a last name but have different first names are typically different people (e.g., spouses, siblings)\"\n- ✅ \"A full name and a first-name-only reference may be the same person\"\n\n---\n\n## Development Notes\n\n- Python 3.10+ required\n- spaCy `en_core_web_lg` model required for NER\n- At least one LLM provider (Ollama, OpenAI, or Anthropic) required for LLM features\n- Current branch: `feature/agent-infrastructure` (Phase 3 complete, Phase 4 planned)\n- `Output/` directory is gitignored but created during analysis\n","numLines":140,"startLine":1,"totalLines":140}}}
