28 mentions) but chapter summaries reference \"Victor Frankenstein\"\n    35→   - Location: Inconsistency between character extraction and chapter character assignment\n    36→   - Fix: Ensure canonical names match across all outputs OR ensure full names are properly aliased\n    37→\n    38→### HIGH\n    39→4. **Massive pronunciation false positives**\n    40→   - Problem: Common English words flagged unnecessarily: \"my\", \"man\", \"father\", \"old\", \"young\", \"mother\", \"girl\", \"woman\", \"creator\", \"stranger\", \"magistrate\", \"Uncle\", \"Child\"\n    41→   - Evidence: 663 total pronunciations include dozens of everyday words that any narrator knows\n    42→   - Location: `src/agents/pronunciation_agent.py` filtering logic\n    43→   - Fix: Implement word frequency filter to exclude common English words (top 5000-10000 most common words)\n    44→\n    45→5. **Missing character: William Frankenstein**\n    46→   - Problem: Victor's younger brother William (murder victim) appears in chapter summaries but not in main character profiles\n    47→   - Evidence: William appears in Chapter 7 character list as \"William Frankenstein\" but is missing from the 15 main character profiles\n    48→   - Location: Character profile generation threshold\n    49→   - Fix: Lower mention threshold or ensure plot-critical characters are always profiled\n    50→\n    51→### MEDIUM\n    52→6. **Ambiguous character entry: \"M.\"**\n    53→   - Problem: Character listed as just \"M.\" with 23 mentions and no description\n    54→   - Evidence: This is likely \"M. Waldman\" or \"M. Krempe\" but listed separately\n    55→   - Location: Name extraction and resolution\n    56→   - Fix: Improve title/abbreviation handling to avoid extracting incomplete names\n    57→\n    58→7. **Duplicate character entries: \"the old man\" vs \"old man\" vs \"De Lacey\"**\n    59→   - Problem: \"the old man\" (19 mentions), \"old man\" (2 mentions), and \"De\" (6 mentions) are separate\n    60→   - Evidence: These likely all refer to De Lacey, the blind father in the cottage\n    61→   - Location: Alias resolution for descriptive references\n    62→   - Fix: Improve resolution of descriptive phrases (\"the old man\") to canonical names\n    63→\n    64→8. **Character split: \"Father\" vs \"my father\"**\n    65→   - Problem: \"Father\" (6 mentions) listed separately from \"my father\" (46 mentions)\n    66→   - Evidence: These are the same character (Alphonse Frankenstein) with different article usage\n    67→   - Location: Canonical name selection\n    68→   - Fix: Normalize \"my X\" and \"X\" and \"the X\" before creating separate entries\n    69→\n    70→### LOW\n    71→9. **Profile confidence issues**\n    72→   - Problem: Elizabeth and Margaret have low confidence (0.30) due to JSON parsing failures\n    73→   - Evidence: Mentioned in pipeline notes\n    74→   - Location: Profile generation LLM output parsing\n    75→   - Fix: Improve JSON extraction robustness or prompt engineering\n    76→\n    77→## Fix History\n    78→### Attempt 1: Fixed CLI output path handling\n    79→**Issue:** CLI ignored explicit `--html` and `--output` flags, creating timestamped directory instead\n    80→\n    81→**Fix Applied:**\n    82→- Modified `src/cli.py` lines 367-368: Added `output_path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)` for JSON output\n    83→- Modified `src/cli.py` lines 397-398: Added `html_path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)` for HTML output\n    84→\n    85→**Testing:** All 444 tests pass.\n    86→\n    87→## Previous Text: gatsby\n    88→- **Result:** FAILED after 5 attempts (4.05/10)\n    89→- **Status:** Marked complete in manifest.json\n    90→\n    91→## Next Action\n    92→Run PROMPT_fix.md to address character alias resolution (Critical #1, #2, #3) and pronunciation false positives (High #4)\n    93→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide ana